{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come on in and sit yourself down. Desperate rain out there, I was half drowned coming from the car park.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (CAREGIVER): We were no better. Stuck behind a tractor the whole way, and the radio had the hurling on full blast.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): I can't hear myself think.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ha, the waiting room telly is no better. Was it a decent match at all?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Limerick got there, just about. Yer man scored a beauty near the end and I nearly missed the turn for the clinic.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): Fair play. Right so, enough of the sport. What has you in today?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Bone pains. Two days.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ah, the bones. How are you in yourself with them?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): I feel like a wet rag.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): Worn out with it?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): Did anything set them off?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): I've overdone it.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Err, he overdid it shifting boxes in the shed on Sunday. The pains are in the arms and the legs.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): And you've had the sickle cell since you were small, isn't that right?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any temperature with this at all?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (CAREGIVER): A small bit. Thirty seven point eight on the thermometer last night. Not raging.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): My feet feel dead.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): Numb in both feet, or just heavy?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): Numb. Both.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain, or trouble getting your breath?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the tummy, any pain or sickness there?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): What are you taking for the sickle cell these days?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Folic acid, 5 milligrams every morning, and the hidroxyurea, 500 milligrams once a day. He doesn't miss them.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): Grand. Any allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll have a quick listen to the chest. It's clear. You're a bit tender along the shins. With the known sickle cell, I think this is a mild pain episode, not a chest crisis.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll get the nurse to take bloods Thursday morning, a full blood count and a reticulocyte count. No need to fast, and take your usual tablets that morning as normal.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): If those come back borderline, we might add a crp. And if the pains haven't settled by the weekend, we might do a chest x-ray.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Umm, for the pain, paracetamol one gram four times a day by mouth, and a good two litres of fluid through the day. I'll see you back here in two weeks. If you're worse before that, don't sit on it, come straight back.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (PATIENT): Ok."
 ],
